    {
      "id": "5f0d106f27b98c30c800bc02743d6787217111a3",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3216631426,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This doesn't really hurt, but this wasn't necessary after 45edc1c3b9905d035732da97dbb0b015231d148e (see that know_all_sci is always false if sci_map is NULL.) In fact, it's possible that Coverity will now come back and say that this is an unnecessary NULL check. ;)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-02T11:18:30.020Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-02T11:18:30.020Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 468234837,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 24092,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c38374f5c1156375188d4ef642740b1f43065e71",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3217035779,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The 45edc1c3b9905d035732da97dbb0b015231d148e change is independent from this MR, as far as I see. This MR changes the code within the same function but end the end of the function.\n\n`sci = wmem_map_lookup(mka_mi_sci_map, mi);`\n\n`wmem_map_lookup()` may return `NULL`, hence sci may be `NULL`.\n\nI think the change will fix the CID.",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-02T13:16:07.893Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-02T13:16:07.893Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 468234837,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 24092,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b0c07aee311e63d2e46195f3634d2b40c88713ae",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3217142154,
          "type": null,
          "body": "`wmem_map_lookup()` cannot return `NULL` there after the change.\n\n`know_all_sci` is set to `false`. It is set to `true` if `sci_map` is non-NULL. It is then set to `false` if `wmem_map_lookup(mka_mi_sci_map, mi);` returns NULL for any of the `mi` added to `mi_array`.\n\nThe second loop isn't entered if `know_all_sci` is `false`, and therefore we know that `wmem_map_lookup(mka_mi_sci_map, mi)` does not return NULL for any `mi` in `mi_array`, since we have not removed any from the array as the loop is immediately afterwards.\n\nBut Coverity may not know that.\n\nThe change was necessary because `know_all_sci` wasn't initially set to false before the change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-02T13:40:49.159Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-02T13:42:16.373Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 468234837,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 24092,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8e76b7aadca9f22cd2772d852c5eec9ced1e8427",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3217245561,
          "type": null,
          "body": "okay, understood. Yeah, following the logic does not allow NULL there, indeed. I agree Coverity may not know that...",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-02T14:03:25.416Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-02T14:03:25.416Z",
